WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:02.939
- [Announcer] This Great
Big Story was made possible

00:00:02.939 --> 00:00:05.683
by Shell. Make the future.

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:08.330
- [Narrator] One man was so inspired

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:10.697
by the science fiction
he consumed as a kid.

00:00:10.697 --> 00:00:12.114
- I am a machine!

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.070
- [Narrator] He dedicated
his life to building robots

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:16.699
that help mankind.

00:00:16.699 --> 00:00:19.616
(futuristic music)

00:00:34.197 --> 00:00:36.790
Yoshiyuki Sankai is the CEO

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:39.380
of the billion dollar company Cyberdyne,

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:40.940
which happens to be the same name

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.533
as the manufacturer of
cyborgs from "The Terminator."

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.270
It took Sankai over two decades

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:58.170
to build an exoskeleton that
uses brain waves to move.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.220
He named the final product HAL,

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:04.780
a name was made famous by the
AI in "2001: A Space Odyssey."

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.510
- Well, that's far safer than allowing HAL

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:07.860
to continue running things.

00:01:14.164 --> 00:01:15.664
- One, two, three.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:44.780
- [Narrator] This technology helps people

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.530
who need it the most,

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:48.523
people like Masami Kawasaki.

00:02:21.326 --> 00:02:24.659
(bright, driving music)

